Naming
******

.[perex]
The `naming` section decides on the letter case of the names you write (classes, methods, functions, constants, enum cases, properties and variables), and on whether the name of an interface or an abstract class includes the word for its kind.

Each kind of name has its own key, and the value is the notation: `PascalCase`, `camelCase`, `UPPER_CASE` or `snake_case`. PSR-1 prescribes only classes, methods and class constants, so the `psr12` and `perCs` standards set only those; Nette Coding Standard sets all of them and writes constants in `PascalCase`.

```neon
naming:
	class: PascalCase
	method: camelCase
	constant: UPPER_CASE
	variable: camelCase
```

A violation is only reported, never fixed: the name of a method or a property would also have to change everywhere it is used, and that cannot be seen from a single file. A name that must stay as it is, such as a method of a stream wrapper that PHP calls by the name `stream_open`, is excluded by a pattern in `naming.except`.

```php .[before]
class Order
{
	public function get_total(): int  // The method `get_total` must be written in camelCase.
	{
		return 0;
	}
}
```


naming.abstractClassAffix
=========================

The word `Abstract` in front of the name of an abstract class, `AbstractFoo`, which is reported and never renamed.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.Classes.SuperfluousAbstractClassNaming` .[decision-facts]


naming.interfaceAffix
=====================

The word `Interface` at the end of the name of an interface, `FooInterface`, which is reported and never renamed.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.Classes.SuperfluousInterfaceNaming` .[decision-facts]


